:: VictoryEnding
<div class="victory-container">

<h1 class="victory-title">VICTORY!</h1>

The four drummers pound their drums with thunderous joy. The sound echoes through every corridor of the palace.

In the dungeons below, the failed suitors grinding chickpeas begin jumping and cheering. "Someone brought the sun! Someone broke the silence! We're FREE!"

The Raja and Rani rush into the chamber, faces alight with happiness.

Princess Chouboli stands frozen, one hand over her mouth, as reality settles upon her. She has spoken four times. The oath is complete.

**She must marry the storyteller.**

Slowly, Chouboli lowers her hand. Her eyes meet the storyteller's—and this time, there's a spark of something new. Respect. Perhaps even... admiration?

"You," she says softly, her fifth word given freely, "are a worthy opponent."

The Raja steps forward, beaming. "The challenge is complete! The marriage shall be arranged!"

</div>

<p class="end-text">
<strong>~ THE END ~</strong>
</p>

<p class="italic-note">
You have successfully made Princess Chouboli speak four times through the power of storytelling and truth.
</p>